<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3521" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ārĕŏla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āri-</span></b> ),
		ae, f.
		dim.
		area. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> (After area, I.)
				<i>A small</i>, <i>open place</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae cenatio areolam aspicit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 5, 6, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ARIOLA,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 584, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(After area, II. E.) <i>A small garden-bed</i>, <i>garden</i>, or <i>cultivated
			place</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 362</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2, 30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">areolae aromatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Cant. 5, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Ezech. 17, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
